  "printed": "John i. 13",
  "page": 361,
  "line": 7,
  "situation": "The third petition drives off two wills the plate never references — John i. 13's *neque ex voluntate carnis, neque ex voluntate viri*. Then it turns the prayer's own geography onto the man saying it: *fiat … de terra hac, quæ ego sum* — thy will be done upon this earth, which I am, the brace holding the clod twice, by this earth and upon it. That is §31's method entire: every clause is made particular before it is asked.",
