   31
  ],
  "printed": "John ix. 31",
  "page": 419,
  "line": 20,
  "situation": "The fourth property of mercy is *fellow-suffering*, and it is not softened. *Though we deserve it, yet He grieveth with us in our calamity* — and the name for it is Zacharias' *tender bowels of His mercy*, the *viscera misericordiæ*, which is an organ and not a sentiment. The close answers a concession made eight leaves back: at 411 the plea had granted that *God heareth not sinners* — John ix. 31, in the mouth of the man born blind. Here: *who not only heareth sinners, but also, in the day of their trouble, those who in the time of their peace despised Him.* The objection is not argued down; it is simply outlived.",
  "source": "identified",
  "band": "R"
 },
