  "printed": "John xx. 23",
  "page": 288,
  "line": 28,
  "situation": "He asks for half of a power that was given whole. John xx. 23 confers both the remitting of sins and the retaining, and the prayer takes the one and expressly declines the other — *sed quoad remissionem, ne ad retentionem, Domine*. Nothing on the page argues the asymmetry; it is enacted rather than defended, as the eleventh-hour stanza above enacts its own and asks the wage of a full day after standing idle through all of it.",
